00:16:32.990 --> 00:16:40.850
But this episode begins with a very famous cold open, the Cheese Puff Cold Open.
但这一集是以一个非常著名的冷开场开始的，就是“芝士球冷开场”。

373
00:16:40.850 --> 00:16:41.590
It is.
确实如此。

374
00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:43.490
I titled it the Cheese Puff.
我把它命名为“芝士球”。

375
00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:46.650
I loved doing this cold open so much.
我太喜欢拍这个冷开场了。

376
00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.370
I have so many questions for you.
我有很多问题想问你。

377
00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:49.790
I have so many questions.
我也有很多问题。

378
00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:51.290
Should we describe it?
我们要描述一下吗？

379
00:16:51.590 --> 00:16:52.370
Describe it.
描述一下吧。

380
00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:53.230
All right.
好的。

381
00:16:53.670 --> 00:17:02.190
It's Pam, Michael, and Ryan tossing Cheese Puffs into one another's mouths in various ways.
就是帕姆、迈克尔和瑞安用各种方式把芝士球扔进对方嘴里。

382
00:17:02.190 --> 00:17:02.670
Right.
对。

383
00:17:02.810 --> 00:17:07.370
It's like the things you see on YouTube of where the guy bounces the basketball off the
就像你在YouTube上看到的那种视频，一个人把篮球从墙上弹开，

384
00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:10.410
back of a wall and it hits the other side of the wall and it goes in the hoop.
撞到墙的另一边，然后弹进篮筐里。

385
00:17:10.790 --> 00:17:11.850
That's what you guys are doing.
你们当时就是在做这个。

386
00:17:11.850 --> 00:17:13.550
But you're doing it with Cheese Puffs.
只不过你们用的是芝士球。

387
00:17:13.690 --> 00:17:19.230
And I love the callback because, remember, this is what Michael took when he ran out of
而且我喜欢这个呼应，因为记得吗，这就是迈克尔最后一天跑出

388
00:17:19.230 --> 00:17:20.950
Dunder Mifflin on that last day.
邓德·米夫林时带走的东西。

389
00:17:21.170 --> 00:17:22.330
You have questions.
你有问题要问。

390
00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:25.230
We got a fan mail flurry about this.
我们收到了很多关于这个的粉丝来信。

391
00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:32.230
So first, we reached out to writer Ryan Coe to find out, like, what was the inspiration
所以首先，我们联系了编剧瑞安·科，想了解一下，这个冷开场的灵感

392
00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:33.410
for this cold open?
是什么？

393
00:17:33.570 --> 00:17:35.630
His response was so funny.
他的回复太搞笑了。

394
00:17:35.790 --> 00:17:36.370
It's so good.
真的太棒了。

395
00:17:36.490 --> 00:17:38.650
I actually spit out my coffee while listening to it.
我听的时候差点把咖啡喷出来。

396
00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:39.690
Yeah, we got to play it.
是啊，我们得放出来听听。

397
00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:40.850
Hi, Jenna.
嗨，珍娜。

398
00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:41.490
Hi, Angela.
嗨，安吉拉。

399
00:17:41.970 --> 00:17:43.890
Thanks for letting me talk about my episode.
谢谢让我聊聊我写的这一集。

400
00:17:44.210 --> 00:17:49.030
Jenna, you had mentioned that you love shooting that cold open with the cheese balls and you
珍娜，你提到过你很喜欢拍那个芝士球的冷开场，而且你

401
00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:50.210
were wondering where it came from.
都在好奇它是怎么来的。

402
00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:54.230
I remember that it was most of all a product of exhaustion.
我记得它主要是精疲力竭的产物。

403
00:17:54.470 --> 00:17:55.390
I'll back up a bit.
我先倒叙一下。

404
00:17:56.070 --> 00:18:01.210
Yeah, you know, for the first draft of my episode, I had written a cold open about how Ryan thought
对，你知道，我那一集的初稿里，写了一个开场戏，讲的是瑞安以为

405
00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:04.010
Pam had a crush on him and no one liked it.
帕姆暗恋他，但大家都不喜欢这个点子。

406
00:18:04.150 --> 00:18:06.190
So it was tossed out and we needed a new cold open.
所以它被弃用了，我们需要一个新的开场戏。

407
00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:09.770
And at this point in the season, all the writers were really exhausted.
当时正值这一季的中段，所有的编剧都非常疲惫。

408
00:18:10.030 --> 00:18:17.730
In season five, as you recall, we did 28 episodes and they were shot in a 10 consecutive
你们可能还记得，第五季我们拍了28集，它们是在连续10周的

409
00:18:17.730 --> 00:18:22.570
weeks of production, then a break so Steve could do a movie, and then 18 straight weeks
制作周期内拍摄的，然后休息了一段时间让史蒂夫去拍电影，接着又是连续18周

410
00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:23.150
of production.
的制作。

411
00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:27.970
Other shows I've been on, I've told them that there was a stretch of 18 straight weeks of
我待过的其他剧组，我告诉他们我们曾有过连续18周的

412
00:18:27.970 --> 00:18:30.490
production and they do not believe we did that.
制作周期，他们根本不相信我们能做到。

413
00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:36.610
In sort of sitcoms, it's more common to do two or three weeks on of production and then
在情景喜剧中，通常是拍两三周

414
00:18:36.610 --> 00:18:41.810
one week off so that the actors can recover and so the writers can catch up and don't get
休息一周，这样演员可以恢复体力，编剧也能赶上进度，不至于

415
00:18:41.810 --> 00:18:42.690
totally burned out.
彻底累垮。

416
00:18:43.050 --> 00:18:45.730
And so 18 straight weeks is a total death march.
所以连续18周简直就是一场死亡行军。

417
00:18:45.730 --> 00:18:50.590
And I remember at that time, a writer was going to go down and check out what was going
我记得当时，有个编剧打算下楼去看看片场

418
00:18:50.590 --> 00:18:51.370
down on set.
发生了什么。

419
00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:54.470
Paul or someone was like, do not go down there.
保罗还是谁说，别去那儿。

420
00:18:54.590 --> 00:18:56.830
The actors are tired and are acting like huge ass.
演员们累坏了，表现得像个混蛋一样。

421
00:18:57.090 --> 00:19:00.230
So yeah, I remember it was a sort of rough time.
所以，是的，我记得那是一段相当艰难的时期。

422
00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:06.450
And so for the last half of season five, we were always behind and I feel like we were
在第五季的后半段，我们总是进度滞后，我觉得我们

423
00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:09.530
working 11 or more hours pretty much every single day.
几乎每天都要工作11个小时甚至更久。

424
00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:15.170
I remember Mindy was really mad that it meant she had no social life and said something
我记得敏迪当时非常生气，因为这意味着她没有社交生活，还说了句

425
00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:17.550
like, I'm going to die alone because of this damn show.
类似“因为这破剧，我注定要孤独终老”的话。

426
00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:23.510
So anyway, we were all very spent and we were trying to come up with a new cold open and
总之，我们都精疲力竭了，当时正试图想出一个新的开场戏，

427
00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:25.530
it was either Aaron Schur or Paul.
要么是亚伦·舒尔，要么是保罗提出来的。

428
00:19:25.830 --> 00:19:29.670
They were both the guys that were really good at making something out of nothing.
他们俩都是那种特别擅长无中生有的人。

429
00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:34.890
One of them said, I don't know, they're throwing cheese balls at each other.
其中一个人说，不知道，就让他们互相扔奶酪球吧。

430
00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:36.410
And everyone's like, great.
大家都说，太棒了。

431
00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:37.430
We don't have to write anything.
我们不用写任何东西了。

432
00:19:37.550 --> 00:19:37.930
That's awesome.
这太赞了。

433
00:19:38.050 --> 00:19:38.190
Okay.
好的。

434
00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:39.470
That's the cold open cheese balls.
这就是奶酪球开场戏的由来。

435
00:19:39.470 --> 00:19:40.290
All right, next.
好了，下一个。

436
00:19:40.810 --> 00:19:45.170
As far as anything else about writing the episode, it was a long time ago and I don't
至于关于写这一集的其他任何事，那已经是很久以前了，我其实

437
00:19:45.170 --> 00:19:47.730
really remember because I was tired.
记不太清了，因为我当时太累了。

438
00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:52.270
Ryan, that made our day.
瑞安，那让我们的一天都变得美好了。

439
00:19:53.570 --> 00:20:00.850
I mean, look at this amazing piece of comedy that came out of just everyone being so tired.
我是说，看看这个精彩的喜剧片段，它竟然诞生于大家如此疲惫的状态下。

440
00:20:01.190 --> 00:20:01.450
Fatigue.
疲劳。

441
00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:02.170
Yes.
没错。

442
00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:09.450
You guys might remember, Ryan is our writer who wiped out while running past the speed reader
你们可能还记得，瑞安就是我们那位在跑过测速仪标志时

443
00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:09.870
sign.
摔倒的编剧。

444
00:20:10.090 --> 00:20:10.430
Yes.
是的。

445
00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:15.670
So Ryan, thank you so much for sharing your memory with us of the cheese ball cold open
所以瑞安，非常感谢你与我们分享关于奶酪球开场戏的记忆，

446
00:20:15.670 --> 00:20:16.230
and now.
现在。

447
00:20:16.350 --> 00:20:18.750
And sorry if we were assholes that week.
还有，抱歉那周我们表现得像个混蛋。

448
00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:19.990
Yeah, sorry.
是啊，抱歉。

449
00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:22.090
I guess we were all tired and grouchy.
我想我们当时都又累又暴躁。

450
00:20:22.290 --> 00:20:23.410
I guess so.
我想也是。

451
00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:26.190
Lady, you said you had some questions.
女士，你说你有几个问题要问。

452
00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:27.510
I do.
我是有。

453
00:20:27.670 --> 00:20:28.830
I'm here to answer questions.
我在这儿就是为了回答问题的。

454
00:20:29.050 --> 00:20:29.390
All right.
好吧。

455
00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:34.510
So I know from other episodes where anytime we had to throw something, you don't get it
我知道在之前的剧集里，每次我们要扔东西的时候，你都不能一次就接住，

456
00:20:34.510 --> 00:20:42.370
on the first take, but that shot of Steve throwing the cheese puff ball at you, you caught
但史蒂夫把芝士球扔向你的那个镜头，你接住了，

457
00:20:42.370 --> 00:20:47.110
it, you chomped it, you looked right to camera, and I was like, my girl, look at her.
你嚼了它，还直接看向镜头，当时我就想，我的姑娘啊，看看她。

458
00:20:47.210 --> 00:20:48.230
I was so proud.
我太骄傲了。

459
00:20:48.350 --> 00:20:52.550
I was like, okay, Sydney Bristow on alias, can you do that?
我当时想，好吧，《双面女间谍》里的悉尼·布里斯托，你能做到吗？

460
00:20:52.810 --> 00:20:54.310
Jenna, this is like your moment.
珍娜，这就是属于你的高光时刻。

461
00:20:54.810 --> 00:20:55.950
All right, I'm going to tell you something.
好吧，我要告诉你一件事。

462
00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:56.430
Okay.
好的。

463
00:20:56.430 --> 00:21:02.170
When I was in high school, I did not have a vibrant social life.
我上高中的时候，社交生活并不丰富。

464
00:21:02.590 --> 00:21:05.430
So you threw cheese balls at your face?
所以你就往自己脸上扔芝士球？

465
00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:06.050
No.
不是。

466
00:21:06.390 --> 00:21:06.690
What?
什么？

467
00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:08.790
I watched a lot of movies.
我看了很多电影。

468
00:21:09.090 --> 00:21:09.330
Okay.
好吧。

469
00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:12.050
And when I watched the movies, I would eat popcorn.
看电影的时候，我会吃爆米花。

470
00:21:12.510 --> 00:21:17.270
And I started throwing the popcorn up in the air and catching it.
然后我就开始把爆米花抛向空中，再用嘴接住。

471
00:21:17.410 --> 00:21:18.030
By yourself?
你自己一个人？

472
00:21:18.270 --> 00:21:18.550
Yeah.
对。

473
00:21:18.770 --> 00:21:19.010
Okay.
好吧。

474
00:21:19.350 --> 00:21:21.490
Listen, it paid off later in my life.
听着，这对我后来的人生很有帮助。

475
00:21:21.490 --> 00:21:22.270
It sure did.
确实很有帮助。

476
00:21:22.470 --> 00:21:22.970
It sure did.
确实很有帮助。

477
00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:24.330
So don't feel sorry for me.
所以别为我感到难过。

478
00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:25.430
I'm not feeling sorry.
我没觉得难过。

479
00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:30.750
I also saw tons of great movies, and I have a great mind for the cinema.
我也看了很多很棒的电影，而且我对电影很有见地。

480
00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:31.850
Yes.
没错。

481
00:21:32.190 --> 00:21:36.150
So I am really good at catching food in my mouth.
所以我真的很擅长用嘴接食物。

482
00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:36.810
I know.
我知道。

483
00:21:37.070 --> 00:21:40.730
Also, my sister and I would throw popcorn at each other.
而且，我和我姐姐以前也会互相扔爆米花。

484
00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:41.310
Sure, sure.
当然，当然。

485
00:21:41.310 --> 00:21:46.050
So when I read this cold open, I was like, I'm going to nail this.
所以当我读到这个开场戏时，我就想，我一定要把它演好。

486
00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:49.690
And then I got really scared that they were going to want to CGI it.
然后我真的很担心他们会想用电脑特效来做。

487
00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:51.170
Because you were like, guys, I got this.
因为你当时说，伙计们，这事儿我能搞定。

488
00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:52.610
It's not CGI.
这不是特效。

489
00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:53.410
No, I know.
不，我知道。

490
00:21:53.590 --> 00:21:55.290
I want everyone to know those are real cheese balls.
我想让大家都知道那是真的芝士球。

491
00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:59.890
We had the best time shooting this.
我们拍这段的时候玩得特别开心。

492
00:22:00.090 --> 00:22:00.970
It looks like it.
看得出来。

493
00:22:00.970 --> 00:22:04.830
But I was just delighted by every moment of it.
但我对其中的每一个瞬间都感到非常高兴。

494
00:22:05.790 --> 00:22:08.030
Jenna, I'm great at catching food in my mouth as well.
珍娜，我也很擅长用嘴接食物。

495
00:22:08.890 --> 00:22:09.250
Oh.
哦。

496
00:22:09.550 --> 00:22:13.170
Just because I have good hand-eye coordination, because I'm a little bit of a sport-o.
只是因为我的手眼协调能力很好，因为我算是个运动健将。

497
00:22:13.250 --> 00:22:15.210
Why have we never thrown food at one another?
为什么我们从来没试过互相扔食物？

498
00:22:15.530 --> 00:22:16.610
What do we have in here?
我们这儿有什么东西吗？

499
