你必须把它背下来。

1003
00:41:50.860 --> 00:41:51.920
You had to read the script.
你必须读剧本。

1004
00:41:51.920 --> 00:41:53.360
You know where the scene is going.
你知道这一幕接下来会发生什么。

1005
00:41:53.620 --> 00:41:53.980
Yes.
是的。

1006
00:41:54.200 --> 00:41:59.560
And so to play all of that, it is like one of the hardest things to do as an actor.
所以要演绎出这一切，对演员来说是最难的事情之一。

1007
00:41:59.800 --> 00:42:02.040
And then to do it comedically, amazing.
而且还要以喜剧的方式演绎，太棒了。

1008
00:42:02.040 --> 00:42:02.480
Amazing.
太棒了。

1009
00:42:02.860 --> 00:42:12.500
We got a fan question about this scene from Kelton O, who said, how is it that Pam and Ryan can hear both sides of this phone call?
我们收到一个关于这一幕的粉丝提问，来自Kelton O，他问，为什么Pam和Ryan能听到这通电话双方的内容？

1010
00:42:12.980 --> 00:42:13.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1011
00:42:13.980 --> 00:42:16.940
They seem to hear Dwight so clearly through the phone.
他们似乎能通过电话清楚地听到Dwight的声音。

1012
00:42:17.480 --> 00:42:23.740
Well, this is very funny, Kelton, because Rain was actually right off camera.
嗯，这很有趣，Kelton，因为Rain其实就在镜头外。

1013
00:42:24.000 --> 00:42:24.560
Yeah.
没错。

1014
00:42:24.740 --> 00:42:26.320
Doing his side of the phone call.
在念他那部分的电话内容。

1015
00:42:26.460 --> 00:42:28.160
We could totally hear him.
我们完全能听到他的声音。

1016
00:42:28.620 --> 00:42:30.340
Rain actually had to come into work that day.
Rain那天其实不得不来上班。

1017
00:42:30.340 --> 00:42:32.120
He did not have anything else to shoot.
他那天没有别的戏要拍。

1018
00:42:32.400 --> 00:42:36.140
All he did was stand off camera and read his side of the phone call.
他所做的就是站在镜头外，念他那部分的电话台词。

1019
00:42:36.700 --> 00:42:37.940
It's actually a thing.
这其实是一种惯例。

1020
00:42:38.120 --> 00:42:39.960
It's called doing off-camera work.
这叫作“画外配音”。

1021
00:42:40.280 --> 00:42:43.340
And that is often how different sides of a phone call are done.
这就是电话两端对话通常的拍摄方式。

1022
00:42:43.600 --> 00:42:49.420
We did not have the capability to, like, call into that office.
我们当时没有那种能力，比如，真的打进那个办公室。

1023
00:42:49.620 --> 00:42:50.000
Right.
对。

1024
00:42:50.300 --> 00:42:51.460
Like we did upstairs.
就像我们在楼上做的那样。

1025
00:42:51.460 --> 00:42:53.800
Because it was a closet and a fakie phone.
因为那只是个储物间，电话也是假的。

1026
00:42:54.000 --> 00:42:54.380
Yes.
没错。

1027
00:42:54.640 --> 00:43:00.040
I thought I could see how they were cheating it a little, because Michael is kind of holding the phone out.
我以为我能看出他们是怎么稍微作弊的，因为Michael当时把电话拿得离耳朵有点远。

1028
00:43:00.040 --> 00:43:05.220
So you would assume if he had the volume pretty high up, it's a tiny room that you guys could probably hear.
所以你会觉得，如果他把音量调得很高，而且那是个很小的房间，你们大概能听到。

1029
00:43:05.440 --> 00:43:08.200
We also had a fan catch from Maya R.
我们还收到了Maya R.发来的粉丝发现。

1030
00:43:08.640 --> 00:43:10.080
Who said this, Angela?
她说这个，Angela？

1031
00:43:10.360 --> 00:43:10.720
What?
什么？

1032
00:43:11.240 --> 00:43:12.900
This went right to my heart.
这直击我的内心。

1033
00:43:13.200 --> 00:43:17.300
She said, I noticed a paper pro stapler on Pam and Ryan's table.
她说，我注意到Pam和Ryan的桌子上有一个Paper Pro订书机。

1034
00:43:17.580 --> 00:43:21.960
And my mom actually works for the company that sells these staplers.
我妈妈正好就在销售这种订书机的公司工作。

1035
00:43:22.580 --> 00:43:27.440
It originated in Pennsylvania before merging with Boss Stitch.
它最初起源于宾夕法尼亚州，后来与Boss Stitch合并了。

1036
00:43:27.720 --> 00:43:30.940
Could this be why the stapler was used in this episode?
这会是这一集里使用这种订书机的原因吗？

1037
00:43:31.900 --> 00:43:36.240
I don't know, Maya, but I brought my paper pro stapler today.
我不知道，Maya，但我今天带了我的Paper Pro订书机来了。

1038
00:43:36.240 --> 00:43:36.740
You did?
你带了？

1039
00:43:36.960 --> 00:43:37.940
I got to try it out.
我得试用一下。

1040
00:43:38.180 --> 00:43:38.580
All right.
好吧。

1041
00:43:39.440 --> 00:43:40.720
I brought champagne.
我带了香槟。

1042
00:43:40.900 --> 00:43:41.820
Jenna brought a stapler.
Jenna带了个订书机。

1043
00:43:42.040 --> 00:43:42.700
Here it is.
在这儿呢。

1044
00:43:43.700 --> 00:43:44.500
Now watch.
现在看好了。

1045
00:43:45.420 --> 00:43:46.740
Do I get to do it?
我可以试一下吗？

1046
00:43:46.860 --> 00:43:47.200
Yes.
可以。

1047
00:43:47.780 --> 00:43:49.740
I am going to do it with a single finger.
我要用一根手指来订。

1048
00:43:49.820 --> 00:43:50.180
Wait, wait.
等等，等等。

1049
00:43:50.340 --> 00:43:50.480
Here.
给你。

1050
00:43:50.600 --> 00:43:52.860
Now, I wish I'd brought a regular stapler.
现在，我真希望我带的是个普通订书机。

1051
00:43:53.000 --> 00:43:54.540
I had meant to bring a regular stapler.
我本来打算带个普通订书机的。

1052
00:43:54.540 --> 00:43:55.640
I'm sure there is one.
我相信肯定有一个。

1053
00:43:55.800 --> 00:43:56.160
Okay, ready?
好了，准备好了吗？

1054
00:43:56.160 --> 00:43:56.540
Watch this.
看这个。

1055
00:43:59.250 --> 00:44:00.730
Can you hear the clicking?
你能听到咔哒声吗？

1056
00:44:00.950 --> 00:44:02.150
Listen to the air pressure.
听听这气压声。

1057
00:44:04.010 --> 00:44:04.950
I heard that.
我听到了。

1058
00:44:05.570 --> 00:44:06.870
It is amazing.
太神奇了。

1059
00:44:07.150 --> 00:44:07.750
Try it.
试试看。

1060
00:44:07.890 --> 00:44:08.730
Okay, I'm going to try it.
好的，我来试试。

1061
00:44:08.810 --> 00:44:09.630
Staple something.
订点什么东西。

1062
00:44:09.850 --> 00:44:10.750
I'm going to staple something.
我要订点什么东西。

1063
00:44:10.750 --> 00:44:13.970
It's not a regular stapler where you get a ka-jung-ka.
它不像普通订书机那样会发出“咔哒”一声。

1064
00:44:14.330 --> 00:44:15.650
It's like, ka-ch.
它听起来像“咔”的一声。

1065
00:44:16.610 --> 00:44:17.930
Okay, that's very hard.
好吧，这太难了。

1066
00:44:17.930 --> 00:44:19.290
You can do it with one finger.
你用一根手指就能做到。

1067
00:44:19.450 --> 00:44:20.110
Okay, ready?
好了，准备好了吗？

1068
00:44:20.310 --> 00:44:20.490
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1069
00:44:21.950 --> 00:44:22.830
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

1070
00:44:23.050 --> 00:44:24.570
I see what you're talking about.
我明白你在说什么了。

1071
00:44:24.710 --> 00:44:26.230
There's like a spring or something.
里面好像有个弹簧之类的东西。

1072
00:44:27.430 --> 00:44:28.050
I see.
我明白了。

1073
00:44:28.230 --> 00:44:28.910
Shut up.
闭嘴。

1074
00:44:29.150 --> 00:44:31.030
I bought you a paper pro stapler.
我给你买了个Paper Pro订书机。

1075
00:44:31.170 --> 00:44:31.290
Yay!
耶！

1076
00:44:31.290 --> 00:44:32.970
Sam, I have one for you.
山姆，我也有一个给你。

1077
00:44:33.230 --> 00:44:33.910
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1078
00:44:34.270 --> 00:44:35.750
Cassie, I have one for you.
凯西，我也有一个给你。

1079
00:44:35.810 --> 00:44:36.010
Wow.
哇。

1080
00:44:36.090 --> 00:44:37.110
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

1081
00:44:37.350 --> 00:44:37.970
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1082
00:44:38.270 --> 00:44:39.390
You need to have it.
你得拥有它。

1083
00:44:39.390 --> 00:44:42.790
But here's the last thing I'll say about the stapler, I think.
但关于这个订书机，我想我最后再说一点。

1084
00:44:43.710 --> 00:44:45.630
I don't think you're done talking about it.
我觉得你还没说完呢。

1085
00:44:45.830 --> 00:44:47.010
Don't make that promise.
别轻易许下这种承诺。

1086
00:44:48.610 --> 00:44:54.590
Sometimes when we do these acting jobs, you acquire a new skill maybe that you didn't have before.
有时候我们做这些表演工作时，可能会学到以前没掌握的新技能。

1087
00:44:54.770 --> 00:44:58.730
When I did Blades of Glory, I had to train with a ice skating coach.
拍《冰刀双人组》的时候，我不得不跟着滑冰教练训练。

1088
00:44:58.910 --> 00:45:01.270
I learned how to be quite a good ice skater.
我学会了怎么滑冰，而且滑得还不错。

1089
00:45:01.490 --> 00:45:01.670
Sure.
当然。

1090
00:45:02.350 --> 00:45:06.430
When I did Walk Hard, I took a little bit of horse riding lessons.
拍《永不止步》的时候，我上过一点骑马课。

1091
00:45:06.810 --> 00:45:07.050
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1092
00:45:07.170 --> 00:45:08.290
It's like a fun perk.
这就像是一种有趣的额外收获。

1093
00:45:08.610 --> 00:45:09.490
You get these skills.
你能获得这些技能。

1094
00:45:09.850 --> 00:45:10.010
Right.
没错。

1095
00:45:10.390 --> 00:45:12.750
Sometimes you get introduced to an item.
有时候你会接触到某样东西。

1096
00:45:13.290 --> 00:45:20.090
I remember when I did Splitting Up Together, there was just this amazing set of pajamas that I'd never heard of before.
我记得拍《分分合合》的时候，有一套很棒的睡衣，我以前从没听说过。

1097
00:45:20.410 --> 00:45:22.750
And after wearing them on the show, I bought three pairs.
在剧里穿过之后，我买了三套。

1098
00:45:22.750 --> 00:45:25.690
I am now a lifelong fan of Sass shoes.
我现在是Sass鞋子的终身粉丝了。

1099
00:45:26.430 --> 00:45:26.930
Exactly.
正是如此。

1100
00:45:27.230 --> 00:45:30.050
That is what this Paper Pro stapler was for me.
这就是这个Paper Pro订书机对我而言的意义。

1101
00:45:30.150 --> 00:45:32.970
And it was all thanks to Michael Scott Paper Company.
这一切都要归功于迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司。

1102
00:45:33.150 --> 00:45:33.810
Well, there you go.
好吧，就是这样。

1103
00:45:34.510 --> 00:45:38.810
Before we go to break, I have one more thing to point out about this scene.
在进入休息时间之前，我还有一点要指出关于这个场景的内容。

1104
00:45:38.990 --> 00:45:40.950
It's at 6 minutes, 11 seconds.
是在6分11秒的时候。

1105
00:45:41.170 --> 00:45:44.070
It is a very good shot of our second goldfish.
那是我们第二条金鱼的一个非常好的镜头。

1106
00:45:44.470 --> 00:45:45.070
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1107
00:45:45.330 --> 00:45:46.970
Our first goldfish was orange.
我们第一条金鱼是橙色的。

1108
00:45:46.970 --> 00:45:48.250
That goldfish is gone.
那条金鱼已经不在了。

1109
00:45:48.250 --> 00:45:52.750
This week, it is a red, orange, white, and black spotted fish.
这周，它变成了一条红、橙、白、黑斑点的鱼。

1110
00:45:53.290 --> 00:45:56.730
And we got a letter from Jess L., who said,
我们收到了一封来自杰斯·L的信，她说，

1111
00:45:56.950 --> 00:46:00.850
I spent 10 years working in pet stores as an aquatic specialist,
我在宠物店做了10年的水族专家，

1112
00:46:00.850 --> 00:46:07.670
and pet industry employees have been wondering for years whether or not the changing of the goldfish were a planned bit.
宠物行业的员工多年来一直想知道金鱼的更换是否是一个预先计划好的桥段。

1113
00:46:07.870 --> 00:46:10.190
Now, we said last week it was.
现在，我们上周说是的。

1114
00:46:10.430 --> 00:46:11.930
But she goes on to say,
但她接着说，

1115
00:46:11.930 --> 00:46:16.250
anyone who works in fish departments knows goldfish deaths are common.
任何在鱼类部门工作的人都知道金鱼死亡是很常见的。

1116
00:46:16.470 --> 00:46:23.490
And a lot of us in the industry assume that the props people chose to make a bit out of the situation.
我们行业里的很多人都认为，是道具组选择利用这种情况来制造一个笑点。

1117
00:46:24.250 --> 00:46:25.730
And just so you know,
而且顺便告诉你们，

1118
00:46:26.770 --> 00:46:29.930
goldfish should have about 10 gallons of water per fish,
金鱼每条应该有大约10加仑的水，

1119
00:46:30.110 --> 00:46:33.250
and it requires filtration to truly thrive in captivity.
并且需要过滤系统才能在人工饲养环境下真正茁壮成长。

1120
00:46:33.770 --> 00:46:36.370
She, I think, wanted us to know that because
我想她之所以想让我们知道这一点，是因为

1121
00:46:36.370 --> 00:46:40.710
any of you out there with goldfish trying to keep them alive, that could really help.
你们中任何养金鱼并试图让它们活下去的人，这真的会有所帮助。

1122
00:46:40.710 --> 00:46:42.670
I think that's solid advice.
我认为这是很中肯的建议。

1123
00:46:43.190 --> 00:46:43.710
All right.
好了。

1124
00:46:43.770 --> 00:46:44.430
That's all I got.
这就是我要说的全部内容。

1125
00:46:44.690 --> 00:46:50.110
Well, I have something delicious coming up with Jim and Andy that I can't wait to share.
嗯，我接下来有个关于吉姆和安迪的精彩片段，迫不及待想和大家分享。

1126
00:46:50.410 --> 00:46:50.670
Ooh.
噢。

1127
00:46:50.890 --> 00:46:53.010
It just brought me so much joy.
它真的带给我太多快乐了。

1128
00:46:53.750 --> 00:46:56.130
And why don't we take a break and I'll come back with that.
我们休息一下，回来后再讲那个片段。

1129
00:46:56.230 --> 00:46:56.850
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

1130
00:46:57.070 --> 00:47:07.740
We are back.
我们回来了。

1131
00:47:07.960 --> 00:47:10.600
I love this Jim and Andy scene.
我喜欢这个吉姆和安迪的场景。

1132
00:47:10.940 --> 00:47:15.380
Jim is going to approach Andy and he's going to say,
吉姆走近安迪，他会说，

1133
00:47:15.520 --> 00:47:16.280
hey, Andy, you know what?
嘿，安迪，你知道吗？

1134
00:47:16.360 --> 00:47:17.600
I've been thinking about what you said.
我一直在想你说的那些话。

1135
00:47:17.920 --> 00:47:19.060
Andy's like, noish.
安迪说，不错嘛。

1136
00:47:20.060 --> 00:47:22.600
And Jim's like, I just don't know if I can do it.
吉姆说，我只是不知道我能不能做到。

1137
00:47:23.160 --> 00:47:27.560
Andy's like, that's interesting because I hear what you're saying is that you want to do it,
安迪说，这很有趣，因为我听出你的意思是你想做，

1138
00:47:27.680 --> 00:47:28.780
which means you can do it.
这意味着你能做到。

1139
00:47:28.940 --> 00:47:32.580
Believe me, I broke up with Angela and I'm like the happiest guy ever.
相信我，我和安吉拉分手了，我现在是世界上最快乐的人。

1140
00:47:32.860 --> 00:47:34.180
I mean, I am so happy.
我是说，我太快乐了。

1141
00:47:34.320 --> 00:47:35.540
I am so happy.
我太快乐了。

1142
00:47:35.800 --> 00:47:37.520
Like total freedom, you know?
就像完全自由了，你懂吗？

1143
00:47:37.880 --> 00:47:40.840
And Jim says, it's just that Pam gets me through the day.
吉姆说，只是帕姆支撑着我度过每一天。

1144
00:47:41.140 --> 00:47:42.600
Like I really rely on her.
我真的很依赖她。

1145
00:47:42.600 --> 00:47:44.440
I'm pretty emotionally needy.
我在情感上挺脆弱的。

1146
00:47:45.260 --> 00:47:47.060
And Andy says, and you know what?
安迪说，你知道吗？

1147
00:47:47.060 --> 00:47:47.820
I'm here for you.
我会支持你的。

1148
00:47:48.020 --> 00:47:50.080
Let me be your traveling pants.
让我做你的“旅行裤”吧。

1149
00:47:50.800 --> 00:47:52.080
That was all scripted.
那全是剧本写好的。

1150
00:47:52.520 --> 00:47:55.940
And in the script, it says that Jim and Andy do a little knuckles bump.
剧本里写着吉姆和安迪碰了碰拳头。

1151
00:47:56.140 --> 00:47:56.400
Yeah.
没错。

1152
00:47:56.540 --> 00:47:58.780
And they just simply say knuckles.
他们就只是简单地说碰拳。

1153
00:47:59.100 --> 00:48:00.520
And that's the end of the scene.
然后这一幕就结束了。

1154
00:48:00.680 --> 00:48:00.920
Okay.
好的。

1155
00:48:00.920 --> 00:48:06.620
Well, in our version, Jim goes to give the knuckles and Andy leans in and puts his cheek
嗯，在我们的版本里，吉姆去碰拳，安迪却凑过来把脸颊

1156
00:48:06.620 --> 00:48:07.720
in front of the knuckles.
贴到了拳头前面。

1157
00:48:08.340 --> 00:48:10.380
And Jim just starts to laugh.
吉姆就开始笑。

1158
00:48:10.600 --> 00:48:13.720
And he's like, dude, you know I meant knuckles.
他说，老兄，你知道我是想碰拳的。

1159
00:48:13.880 --> 00:48:14.800
And he's like, yeah, knuckles.
安迪就说，对啊，碰拳。

1160
00:48:15.480 --> 00:48:15.860
All right.
好吧。

1161
00:48:16.100 --> 00:48:17.740
So Ed just improvised that.
所以那是艾德即兴发挥的。

1162
00:48:17.900 --> 00:48:19.000
That whole moment.
整个那一刻。

1163
00:48:19.260 --> 00:48:21.500
Go to eight minutes, 26 seconds.
跳到八分二十六秒。

1164
00:48:21.820 --> 00:48:27.020
John is laughing at Ed because he didn't know Ed was going to lean his face into the knuckle
约翰在笑艾德，因为他不知道艾德会把脸凑到拳头

1165
00:48:27.020 --> 00:48:27.380
bump.
上。

1166
00:48:27.860 --> 00:48:29.160
And it made it in.
而这一幕被保留了下来。

1167
00:48:29.300 --> 00:48:32.160
And it just brought me joy because I just see these two guys.
这让我感到很开心，因为我看到了这两个人。

1168
00:48:32.160 --> 00:48:35.380
And I see their friendship at eight minutes, 26 seconds.
在八分二十六秒，我看到了他们的友谊。

1169
00:48:35.840 --> 00:48:40.860
Well, when Andy said, I'll be your traveling pants, that made me think of our director,
嗯，当安迪说，我会成为你的牛仔裤时，让我想起了我们的导演，

1170
00:48:40.940 --> 00:48:44.420
Ken Kwapis, who directed The Sisterhood of the Traveling Pants.
肯·卡皮斯，他执导了《牛仔裤的夏天》。

1171
00:48:44.420 --> 00:48:44.800
Yes.
是的。

1172
00:48:44.900 --> 00:48:47.060
And you and I went together to go see it.
而且你和我还一起去看了那部电影。

1173
00:48:47.200 --> 00:48:51.640
I remember watching that movie because there was this really handsome.
我记得看那部电影是因为里面有个非常帅的……

1174
00:48:52.500 --> 00:48:53.940
It made us want to go to Greece.
它让我们想去希腊。

1175
00:48:54.140 --> 00:48:56.420
Remember after that movie, we're like, we should go to Greece.
记得看完那部电影后，我们说，我们应该去希腊。

1176
00:48:56.680 --> 00:48:57.280
We really should.
我们真的应该去。

1177
00:48:57.380 --> 00:48:58.420
We should still go to Greece.
我们还是应该去希腊。

1178
00:48:58.440 --> 00:48:58.860
We should.
我们应该去。

1179
00:48:59.300 --> 00:49:02.060
Well, now we have another scene out by the dumpster.
好吧，现在我们在垃圾桶旁边还有另一场戏。

1180
00:49:02.960 --> 00:49:05.020
Michael is going to meet Dwight again.
迈克尔又要去见德怀特了。

1181
00:49:05.020 --> 00:49:05.820
But guess what?
但你猜怎么着？

1182
00:49:06.500 --> 00:49:07.420
It's a setup.
这是个陷阱。

1183
00:49:08.100 --> 00:49:08.380
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1184
00:49:08.700 --> 00:49:09.620
Charles is there.
查尔斯也在那儿。

1185
00:49:09.820 --> 00:49:10.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1186
00:49:10.180 --> 00:49:15.680
And Charles is going to tell Michael to leave Dunder Mifflin alone and to stop pestering Dwight
查尔斯要告诉迈克尔离邓德·米夫林远点，别再纠缠德怀特

1187
00:49:15.680 --> 00:49:16.480
for info.
打听消息了。

1188
00:49:16.800 --> 00:49:19.000
I have two things to point out about this scene.
关于这场戏，我有两点要指出。

1189
00:49:19.140 --> 00:49:19.740
What are they?
是哪两点？

1190
00:49:20.020 --> 00:49:22.300
The first one is from the shooting draft script.
第一点来自拍摄剧本。

1191
00:49:22.300 --> 00:49:24.780
And it's something that did not make it in the episode.
那是最终没能出现在剧集里的内容。

1192
00:49:24.780 --> 00:49:26.280
And I really wish it had.
我真希望它能保留下来。

1193
00:49:27.100 --> 00:49:29.580
Michael immediately notices Dwight's shirt.
迈克尔立刻注意到了德怀特的衬衫。

1194
00:49:29.980 --> 00:49:30.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1195
00:49:30.500 --> 00:49:30.920
Yeah.
没错。

1196
00:49:31.100 --> 00:49:34.060
And he says, why are you dressed like that?
他说，你为什么穿成那样？

1197
00:49:34.180 --> 00:49:37.100
And he turns to Charles and goes, are you making him wear that?
然后他转向查尔斯说，是你让他穿成这样的吗？

1198
00:49:37.240 --> 00:49:38.620
What about his attack readiness?
那他的攻击准备状态怎么办？

1199
00:49:38.620 --> 00:49:39.480
You fool.
你这个傻瓜。

1200
00:49:40.120 --> 00:49:41.900
Oh, what a great callback.
哦，多棒的呼应啊。

1201
00:49:42.080 --> 00:49:42.660
I know.
我知道。

1202
00:49:42.660 --> 00:49:44.940
I thought it was so sweet that Michael was like, oh, yeah.
我觉得迈克尔那种“哦，是啊”的态度特别可爱。

1203
00:49:44.940 --> 00:49:47.180
Dwight has to wear short sleeves so he can attack someone.
德怀特必须穿短袖，这样他才能随时攻击别人。

1204
00:49:47.400 --> 00:49:47.680
Yes.
是的。

1205
00:49:48.100 --> 00:49:51.480
I had asked James Carey if he would send me the call sheets for this episode.
我曾问过詹姆斯·凯里能不能把这一集的通告单发给我。

1206
00:49:51.480 --> 00:49:53.560
There were a few things I wanted to investigate.
有几件事我想调查一下。

1207
00:49:54.720 --> 00:50:01.900
And I noticed that there was a note for this scene that said, we need to shoot this scene
我注意到这一场戏的备注里写着，我们必须在下午三点半拍摄这场戏，

1208
00:50:01.900 --> 00:50:03.460
at 3.30 p.m.
下午三点半，

1209
00:50:03.660 --> 00:50:05.200
with three exclamation points.
后面还加了三个感叹号。

1210
00:50:06.020 --> 00:50:07.380
I asked Randy about this.
我问过兰迪这件事。

1211
00:50:07.480 --> 00:50:07.720
Why?
为什么？

1212
00:50:08.460 --> 00:50:08.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1213
00:50:08.980 --> 00:50:10.420
Did Idris have to go somewhere?
是伊德里斯有什么急事要走吗？

1214
00:50:10.800 --> 00:50:11.640
Why 3.30?
为什么是三点半？

1215
00:50:11.860 --> 00:50:12.020
What was it?
到底是怎么回事？

1216
00:50:12.480 --> 00:50:14.680
He said it was the light.
他说是因为光线。

1217
00:50:14.940 --> 00:50:15.440
Ah.
啊。

1218
00:50:15.780 --> 00:50:21.300
That this section of the alleyway was on the far side of stage two, and it was kind
他说那段小巷位于二号摄影棚的最远端，

1219
00:50:21.300 --> 00:50:25.260
of a deep canyon, he said, between the stage and the hedges.
就像是摄影棚和树篱之间的一道深谷。

1220
00:50:25.520 --> 00:50:28.800
It was on the far side of the warehouse where we filmed the warehouse scenes.
就在我们拍摄仓库戏份的仓库那一侧的最远端。

1221
00:50:28.980 --> 00:50:29.300
Yes.
没错。

1222
00:50:29.600 --> 00:50:34.400
And he said it's really, really difficult to hide lights there, so you have to use natural
他说在那里藏灯光真的非常非常困难，所以必须利用自然光。

1223
00:50:34.400 --> 00:50:34.740
light.
如果拍得太早或太晚，太阳就会被树篱或仓库挡住。

1224
00:50:34.900 --> 00:50:42.040
And if you shoot it too early or too late, the sun is blocked by the hedges or by the warehouse.
但我想在三点半的时候，角度刚好合适。

1225
00:50:42.040 --> 00:50:45.900
But I guess at 3.30, the angle is just right.
所以我猜我们的鸟儿葬礼也是在三点半拍的？

1226
00:50:46.260 --> 00:50:49.240
So I guess at 3.30 is when we had our bird funeral?
肯定是的。

1227
00:50:49.860 --> 00:50:50.940
It must have been.
三点半，在小巷里。

1228
00:50:51.100 --> 00:50:52.300
3.30 in the alley.
我在想我在那条小巷里拍过多少场戏。

1229
00:50:52.600 --> 00:50:55.260
I am thinking of how many scenes I had in that alley.
那是安吉拉和德怀特见面的地方，她给了他一份给斯普林克尔斯用的药膏清单，

1230
00:50:55.520 --> 00:51:00.540
That's where Angela and Dwight would meet, and she gave him Sprinkles' list of ointments
还有诸如此类的东西。

1231
00:51:00.540 --> 00:51:01.600
and things like that.
多年以后，我还在那里说过爵士乐很蠢。

1232
00:51:01.680 --> 00:51:04.500
And years later, that's where I say jazz is stupid.
那肯定也是在三点半拍的。

1233
00:51:04.500 --> 00:51:06.300
Must have been at 3.30.
三点半，在小巷里。

1234
00:51:06.360 --> 00:51:07.400
3.30 in the alley.
你都可以按这个时间来对表了。

1235
00:51:07.580 --> 00:51:08.760
You can set your watch by it.
好吧，迈克尔要回到迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司，他打算告诉他们发生了什么。

1236
00:51:09.080 --> 00:51:12.700
Well, Michael's going to return to Michael Scott Paper Company, and he's going to try
基本上，就是有人往他脸上扔了一个装满尿的水气球。

1237
00:51:12.700 --> 00:51:13.760
to tell them what happened.
这就是他告诉帕姆和瑞安的内容。

1238
00:51:14.020 --> 00:51:18.080
And basically, he got a pee-filled water balloon thrown in his face.
是的。

1239
00:51:18.220 --> 00:51:19.720
That's what he tells Pam and Ryan.
我是说，显然他生命中的某个时刻真的发生过这种事，对吧？

1240
00:51:20.160 --> 00:51:20.640
Yes.
肯定发生过。

1241
00:51:21.300 --> 00:51:26.320
I mean, clearly at some point in his life that actually happened, right?
哦，那太糟糕了。

1242
00:51:26.800 --> 00:51:27.600
Must have.
好吧，他们得好好解读一下那是什么意思，才能弄清楚到底发生了什么鬼事。

1243
00:51:27.840 --> 00:51:28.740
Oh, that's terrible.
迈克尔要给德怀特打电话，他说，我要抢走你所有的客户，

1244
00:51:29.400 --> 00:51:34.240
Well, they have to really decipher what that means so they can figure out what the heck
还要当着你的面干掉他们。

1245
00:51:34.240 --> 00:51:34.760
is happening.
是啊。

1246
00:51:35.100 --> 00:51:40.360
Well, Michael's going to call Dwight, and he says, I'm going to steal all your clients,
有点太激烈了。

1247
00:51:40.520 --> 00:51:42.000
and I'm going to kill them in front of you.
我要向你发起攻击，而且会来势汹汹。

1248
00:51:42.240 --> 00:51:42.500
Yeah.
是的。

1249
00:51:42.680 --> 00:51:43.580
It's a little intense.
我当时问过詹姆斯·凯里能不能把这一集的通告单发给我。

1250
00:51:43.580 --> 00:51:46.120
I'm going to come at you, and I'm going to come at you hard.
有几件事我想调查一下。

1251
00:51:47.180 --> 00:51:52.640
And then both Dwight and Michael try to call Dwight's biggest client, the whale, Mr.
然后德怀特和迈克尔都试图给德怀特最大的客户，也就是那条大鱼，斯科菲尔德先生打电话。

1252
00:51:53.020 --> 00:51:53.420
Schofield.
斯科菲尔德。

1253
00:51:55.540 --> 00:51:56.340
From HarperCollins.
来自哈珀柯林斯出版社。

1254
00:51:57.840 --> 00:52:01.460
HarperCollins, who is publishing our book, Office BFF.
哈珀柯林斯，就是我们要出版的书《办公室死党》的出版社。

1255
00:52:01.760 --> 00:52:02.180
I know.
我知道。

1256
00:52:02.340 --> 00:52:05.720
Jenna, when I re-watched this, I was like, oh my gosh, this is synchronicity.
珍娜，当我重温这一集时，我心想，天哪，这真是巧合。

1257
00:52:05.980 --> 00:52:09.120
Does this mean our book is going to be printed on Dunder Mifflin paper?
这是否意味着我们的书会印在邓德·米夫林公司的纸上？

1258
00:52:09.600 --> 00:52:10.080
What?
什么？

1259
00:52:10.520 --> 00:52:12.100
That would be amazing.
那太棒了。

1260
00:52:12.580 --> 00:52:15.540
I mean, they're a client, right?
我是说，他们是客户，对吧？

1261
00:52:16.040 --> 00:52:19.260
Our book is being published on the East CoaSt.
我们的书是在东海岸出版的。

1262
00:52:19.700 --> 00:52:24.640
It was really cool, though, because of all the book publishers out there, we're with HarperCollins,
不过这真的很酷，因为在所有的图书出版商中，我们选择了哈珀柯林斯，

1263
00:52:24.640 --> 00:52:27.840
and then Dwight says HarperCollins, and I was like, oh my God.
然后德怀特提到了哈珀柯林斯，我当时就想，天哪。

1264
00:52:28.060 --> 00:52:28.560
I know.
我知道。

1265
00:52:29.020 --> 00:52:31.020
Should we give a book update, by the way?
顺便问一下，我们要更新一下书的进度吗？

1266
00:52:31.080 --> 00:52:34.880
I want everyone to know we made it through that crazy document.
我想让大家知道我们已经完成了那份疯狂的文件。

1267
00:52:35.240 --> 00:52:36.240
I figured it out.
我搞定了。

1268
00:52:36.480 --> 00:52:37.660
Angela figured it out.
安吉拉搞定了。

1269
00:52:37.680 --> 00:52:38.400
That's saying something.
这可真不容易。

1270
00:52:38.520 --> 00:52:38.980
Listen, Jenna.
听着，珍娜。

1271
00:52:38.980 --> 00:52:42.220
She didn't think she was going to figure it out, and I said, you can do it.
她当时觉得她搞不定，但我说，你能行的。

1272
00:52:42.280 --> 00:52:46.700
I really had a moment, you guys, like for real, where I was like, this isn't going to
伙计们，我真的有过那么一刻，说真的，我当时想，这事儿肯定

1273
00:52:46.700 --> 00:52:48.280
happen, and I'm sorry.
成不了，我很抱歉。

1274
00:52:49.000 --> 00:52:50.200
I can't do it.
我做不到。

1275
00:52:50.320 --> 00:52:51.260
But then I did it.
但后来我做到了。

1276
00:52:51.340 --> 00:52:51.960
You did it.
你做到了。

1277
00:52:52.500 --> 00:52:56.460
I made myself a little cheat sheet that I kept by my computer.
我给自己做了一份小抄，一直放在电脑旁边。

1278
00:52:56.900 --> 00:52:57.480
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

1279
00:52:57.800 --> 00:52:59.800
I mean, listen, I hope I did it.
我是说，听着，我希望我做对了。

1280
00:53:00.020 --> 00:53:00.480
I know.
我知道。

1281
00:53:00.560 --> 00:53:02.180
We haven't gotten any feedback on it yet.
我们还没收到任何反馈。

1282
00:53:02.220 --> 00:53:05.300
Yeah, maybe we're going to get a note back that was like, well, way to go, ladies.
是啊，也许我们会收到回复说，干得好，女士们。

1283
00:53:05.300 --> 00:53:06.660
You completely effed it up.
你们彻底搞砸了。

1284
00:53:06.800 --> 00:53:07.320
I know.
我知道。

1285
00:53:07.880 --> 00:53:13.420
And, okay, so we have two more rounds of that, and then the book is locked, and it goes to
好吧，我们还有两轮修改，然后书稿就定稿了，接着送去

1286
00:53:13.420 --> 00:53:13.900
the printer.
印刷厂。

1287
00:53:14.140 --> 00:53:14.980
Oh, Lordy.
天哪。

1288
00:53:15.460 --> 00:53:16.120
So, yeah.
所以，是的。

1289
00:53:16.360 --> 00:53:17.320
Can't make any changes.
不能再做任何改动了。

1290
00:53:17.960 --> 00:53:18.460
I know.
我知道。

1291
00:53:18.780 --> 00:53:19.700
It's coming up.
快要完成了。

1292
00:53:20.340 --> 00:53:21.760
I showed it to my kids.
我给我的孩子们看了。

1293
00:53:22.280 --> 00:53:22.600
Yeah?
是吗？

1294
00:53:22.860 --> 00:53:25.880
I showed them the photo layout, and they were like, oh, my gosh, because it's finally
我给他们看了照片排版，他们说，天哪，因为它终于

1295
00:53:25.880 --> 00:53:26.820
a book.
像本书了。

1296
00:53:26.960 --> 00:53:27.520
Do you know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1297
00:53:27.540 --> 00:53:27.740
Yes.
明白。

1298
00:53:27.740 --> 00:53:29.940
It's not just like you and I turning in all these pages.
这不仅仅是你和我交上去的那些页面。

1299
00:53:30.280 --> 00:53:30.600
Yes.
是的。

1300
00:53:30.940 --> 00:53:32.100
It looks like a book.
它看起来就像本书。

1301
00:53:32.100 --> 00:53:33.080
It looks like a book.
看起来像本书。

1302
00:53:33.080 --> 00:53:34.060
Visually in a PDF.
视觉上是PDF格式的。

1303
00:53:34.880 --> 00:53:40.240
I showed it to Lee, and I said, oh, do you want to see how the photos kind of lay out?
我把它给李看了，我说，噢，你想看看这些照片是怎么排版的吗？

1304
00:53:40.420 --> 00:53:42.020
And I thought he would look at it.
我以为他会看一眼。

1305
00:53:42.120 --> 00:53:43.400
Honestly, I thought he would like-
老实说，我以为他会……

1306
00:53:43.400 --> 00:53:44.520
Just glance at it.
只是扫一眼。

1307
00:53:44.540 --> 00:53:44.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1308
00:53:44.760 --> 00:53:46.160
Then he would be like, oh, my God, it looks cool.
然后他会说，天哪，看起来真酷。

1309
00:53:46.160 --> 00:53:48.680
He went through every single page.
结果他把每一页都翻了一遍。

1310
00:53:48.840 --> 00:53:50.280
But he was compelled to.
但他就是忍不住要看。

1311
00:53:50.360 --> 00:53:52.820
He was like, this is amazing.
他说，这太棒了。

1312
00:53:53.040 --> 00:53:53.380
Aw.
噢。

1313
00:53:53.840 --> 00:53:54.660
He was like-
他说……

1314
00:53:54.660 --> 00:53:56.240
Dr. Thibodeau, Lee said amazing.
蒂博多医生，李说这太棒了。

1315
00:53:56.460 --> 00:53:57.440
Lee said amazing.
李说这太棒了。

1316
00:53:57.800 --> 00:54:00.640
He said, it's so personal.
他说，这太私人化了。

1317
00:54:01.160 --> 00:54:02.160
It's wow.
真是太赞了。

1318
00:54:02.300 --> 00:54:03.980
He's like, these pictures.
他说，这些照片……

1319
00:54:04.540 --> 00:54:06.420
He already knew the stories.
他本来就知道这些故事。

1320
00:54:06.820 --> 00:54:07.180
Right.
没错。

1321
00:54:07.680 --> 00:54:10.900
And he just was like, people are going to love this.
他当时就说，大家一定会喜欢这个的。

1322
00:54:11.040 --> 00:54:11.580
That's what he said.
他就是这么说的。

1323
00:54:11.600 --> 00:54:15.260
And it meant so much to me because we've, you know, sometimes you make something in a
这对我很重要，因为你知道，有时候你在一个

1324
00:54:15.260 --> 00:54:16.420
bubble and you don't know.
封闭的环境里创作，你心里没底。

1325
00:54:16.620 --> 00:54:16.900
Right.
没错。

1326
00:54:17.180 --> 00:54:18.080
We like it.
我们自己喜欢。

1327
00:54:18.120 --> 00:54:18.900
We love it.
