01:06:34.980 --> 01:06:35.860
That's great.
兰迪还想让你知道，尼古拉餐厅有整个山谷里最好吃的切碎沙拉。

1645
01:06:36.200 --> 01:06:41.900
Randy would also like you to know that Nicola's has the best chopped salad in the valley.
我查过了。

1646
01:06:42.240 --> 01:06:43.020
I looked it up.
看起来真的很不错，而且只要16美元。

1647
01:06:43.200 --> 01:06:45.420
It looks really good and it costs $16.
我现在真想来一份切碎沙拉。

1648
01:06:46.040 --> 01:06:47.800
I would love a chopped salad right now.
我知道。

1649
01:06:47.920 --> 01:06:48.420
I know.
我们待会儿就去吃那个吧。

1650
01:06:48.700 --> 01:06:49.980
That's what we should do after.
没错。

1651
01:06:50.200 --> 01:06:51.740
Let's swing by Nicola's or something.
我们要不去Nicola's转转或者干点别的。

1652
01:06:51.960 --> 01:06:52.660
And have a chopped salad?
去吃个切碎沙拉？

1653
01:06:52.760 --> 01:06:53.400
Have a chopped salad.
吃个切碎沙拉。

1654
01:06:53.660 --> 01:06:59.200
Well, in order to shoot this scene, we had to get there at 6.30 in the morning and we
为了拍这场戏，我们得在早上6点半赶到那儿，而且我们

1655
01:06:59.200 --> 01:07:03.500
had to shoot at 7.30 because we had to do it before the restaurant was open.
必须在7点半开拍，因为得在餐厅开门前拍完。

1656
01:07:04.320 --> 01:07:06.880
But after this, BJ and I just got to go home.
但拍完之后，我和BJ就能直接回家了。

1657
01:07:06.960 --> 01:07:08.000
That's all I had to do that day.
那天我就只有这点工作。

1658
01:07:08.080 --> 01:07:09.760
I remember I was back home by like 10 a.m.
我记得大概早上10点我就到家了。

1659
01:07:09.900 --> 01:07:11.120
My work day was done.
我的工作日就结束了。

1660
01:07:11.960 --> 01:07:14.820
Steve and the rest of the crew did a whole day of locations.
史蒂夫和剧组其他人还得在外景地忙活一整天。

1661
01:07:15.280 --> 01:07:21.140
But while I was looking at the call sheet, I saw this fascinating detail, which was the
但我在看通告单的时候，发现了一个有趣的细节，就是

1662
01:07:21.140 --> 01:07:22.200
van schedule.
面包车时刻表。

1663
01:07:22.720 --> 01:07:23.060
Ooh.
噢。

1664
01:07:23.060 --> 01:07:27.120
Do you remember these van schedules when we would shoot on location, lady?
你还记得我们外景拍摄时的那些面包车时刻表吗，女士？

1665
01:07:27.720 --> 01:07:28.080
No.
不记得。

1666
01:07:28.620 --> 01:07:29.340
You don't?
你不记得？

1667
01:07:29.420 --> 01:07:33.960
Oh, see, this is the thing I used to love to do where I read every detail of a call sheet.
你看，我以前最喜欢做的事就是阅读通告单上的每一个细节。

1668
01:07:34.140 --> 01:07:34.640
Yes, you would.
没错，你确实会看。

1669
01:07:35.120 --> 01:07:37.760
I would show up and be like, why is Access Hollywood here?
我到现场会问，为什么《好莱坞娱乐新闻》的人在这儿？

1670
01:07:37.880 --> 01:07:39.840
And you'd be like, Angela, it's on the call sheet.
然后你就会说，安吉拉，通告单上写着呢。

1671
01:07:40.200 --> 01:07:43.280
And they put a memo in your trailer probably last week.
而且他们可能上周就往你房车里塞备忘录了。

1672
01:07:43.480 --> 01:07:44.140
I stepped right over that piece of paper.
我直接从那张纸上跨过去了。

1673
01:07:44.140 --> 01:07:44.780
She really would.
她真的会那样。

1674
01:07:44.920 --> 01:07:46.840
There'd be a pile of memos on her floor.
她房车地板上总有一堆备忘录。

1675
01:07:47.020 --> 01:07:47.800
I'd kick the papers to the side.
我会把那些纸踢到一边。

1676
01:07:47.980 --> 01:07:48.340
All right.
好吧。

1677
01:07:48.340 --> 01:07:53.080
So when you shoot on location, you park your car, and they have the hair and makeup trailers
所以当你在外景拍摄时，你停好车，他们会把发型和化妆房车

1678
01:07:53.080 --> 01:07:55.500
in a big parking lot, and they call it base camp.
停在一个大停车场里，他们管这叫大本营。

1679
01:07:56.000 --> 01:07:58.680
This is where the caterers will set up their food tent.
这是餐饮人员搭建食品帐篷的地方。

1680
01:07:58.680 --> 01:07:59.840
It's where you eat lunch.
也是你吃午饭的地方。

1681
01:08:00.280 --> 01:08:05.140
But a lot of times, base camp is really far away from the actual shooting location, and
但很多时候，大本营离实际拍摄地点非常远，

1682
01:08:05.140 --> 01:08:06.420
that was the case here.
这次就是这种情况。

1683
01:08:06.580 --> 01:08:12.200
It was about a 15-minute van ride to get from base camp to Nicola's restaurant.
从大本营坐面包车到Nicola's餐厅大约需要15分钟。

1684
01:08:12.660 --> 01:08:17.240
So they had to have a van schedule to shuttle all of these people to set.
所以他们必须安排一个面包车时刻表，把所有人接送到片场。

1685
01:08:17.240 --> 01:08:18.680
And here's what it said.
上面是这么写的。

1686
01:08:18.940 --> 01:08:25.640
It said breakfast would be available as of 515, and then you could take one of six vans
上面写着5点15分提供早餐，然后你可以乘坐六班车中的一班

1687
01:08:25.640 --> 01:08:26.240
to set.
前往片场。

1688
01:08:26.700 --> 01:08:35.540
They left at 542 a.m., 6 a.m., 612 a.m., and they designated this van for our grip and
发车时间分别是早上5点42分、6点、6点12分，他们把这班车指定给灯光和

1689
01:08:35.540 --> 01:08:44.040
electric crew, 630 a.m., and then there was one last van at 642 a.m., and in all caps,
电力组，6点30分，然后最后一班车是6点42分，而且用全大写字母

1690
01:08:44.240 --> 01:08:45.860
it said, this is the late van.
写着：这是末班车。

1691
01:08:46.520 --> 01:08:48.300
You did not want to be on the late van.
你绝对不想坐上那班末班车。

1692
01:08:48.440 --> 01:08:48.600
Don't do it.
千万别坐。

1693
01:08:49.100 --> 01:08:49.740
No, no, no, no.
不，不，不，不。

1694
01:08:50.080 --> 01:08:55.260
There were also additional shuttles for the cast and the background actors that were set
另外还有为演员和群演准备的接送车，

1695
01:08:55.260 --> 01:08:56.680
to leave at 7 a.m.
定于早上7点出发。

1696
01:08:57.080 --> 01:09:01.180
So the idea was the crew would get there, set up all the lights, and then the actors would
所以计划是剧组先到，架好所有灯光，然后演员再

1697
01:09:01.180 --> 01:09:01.560
land.
抵达。

1698
01:09:01.720 --> 01:09:03.900
The hair and makeup folks would ride with the actors.
发型和化妆师会和演员同车。

1699
01:09:04.280 --> 01:09:05.360
That's the van schedule.
这就是面包车时刻表。

1700
01:09:05.640 --> 01:09:08.180
That was Randy's job to make that van schedule.
制定那个时刻表是兰迪的工作。

1701
01:09:08.340 --> 01:09:09.500
He did a fantastic job.
他干得太棒了。

1702
01:09:09.500 --> 01:09:12.000
So Dwight never makes it to the restaurant.
所以德怀特根本没去成那家餐厅。

1703
01:09:12.000 --> 01:09:13.680
He calls and says he hit a bear.
他打电话说他撞到了一头熊。

1704
01:09:14.240 --> 01:09:16.960
And Michael just believes it.
而迈克尔居然就信了。

1705
01:09:17.100 --> 01:09:18.100
Not just Michael.
不只是迈克尔。

1706
01:09:18.440 --> 01:09:21.520
I will have you know that Pam and Ryan don't even raise an eyebrow.
我得告诉你，帕姆和瑞安连眼皮都没抬一下。

1707
01:09:21.740 --> 01:09:26.300
They don't even look up from their menu when Michael says, Dwight hit a bear, but he's
当迈克尔说“德怀特撞到熊了，但他正在赶来”时，

1708
01:09:26.300 --> 01:09:26.840
on the way.
他们甚至都没从菜单上抬起头来。

1709
01:09:27.260 --> 01:09:29.000
How many bears has Dwight hit?
德怀特到底撞过多少次熊？

1710
01:09:29.200 --> 01:09:30.920
Why is this so believable?
为什么这事儿这么可信？

1711
01:09:31.540 --> 01:09:33.580
They get back to Michael Scott Paper Company.
他们回到迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司。

1712
01:09:33.920 --> 01:09:35.500
They discover they've been robbed.
发现他们被抢了。

1713
01:09:35.880 --> 01:09:36.620
Dwight calls.
德怀特打来电话。

1714
01:09:36.800 --> 01:09:38.940
Michael is like, I don't have time to talk.
迈克尔说，我没时间跟你废话。

1715
01:09:39.080 --> 01:09:40.080
We've been robbed.
我们被抢了。

1716
01:09:40.940 --> 01:09:44.380
And once again, Pam and Ryan are like, it was Dwight.
而帕姆和瑞安又一次觉得，肯定是德怀特干的。

1717
01:09:44.720 --> 01:09:45.100
Yeah.
没错。

1718
01:09:45.540 --> 01:09:49.220
This is when Dwight is going to start poaching the clients off the Rolodex.
这时候德怀特开始从通讯录里挖客户了。

1719
01:09:49.360 --> 01:09:53.840
And to get back at him, Michael is going to eat his meatball parm that he brought back
为了报复他，迈克尔要吃掉德怀特给他带回来的肉丸帕尔马干酪三明治，

1720
01:09:53.840 --> 01:09:55.620
for him, which is so funny.
这太搞笑了。

1721
01:09:55.760 --> 01:09:57.980
He goes, Dwight says, I knew you were going to do that.
他说，德怀特说，我就知道你会这么做。

1722
01:09:58.120 --> 01:09:59.940
And that's why I made you order it.
所以我才让你点这个。

1723
01:09:59.940 --> 01:10:01.800
Because it's the worst thing on their menu.
因为这是他们菜单上最难吃的东西。

1724
01:10:02.440 --> 01:10:05.160
And then the way Steve is so disgusted by it.
还有史蒂夫表现出的那种厌恶感。

1725
01:10:05.300 --> 01:10:09.200
Why is it so funny to watch Steve eat food that he's disgusted with?
为什么看史蒂夫吃他觉得恶心的食物会这么好笑？

1726
01:10:09.320 --> 01:10:09.500
Anything with food.
任何跟食物有关的都行。

1727
01:10:09.660 --> 01:10:10.380
It's hilarious.
太搞笑了。

1728
01:10:10.740 --> 01:10:13.120
Well, in Casual Friday, he's going to eat everybody's lunch.
嗯，在“休闲星期五”那一集里，他要把所有人的午餐都吃掉。

1729
01:10:13.120 --> 01:10:14.040
And it's very, very funny.
那真的非常、非常搞笑。

1730
01:10:14.140 --> 01:10:15.000
I can't wait to get to that.
我迫不及待想讲到那儿了。

1731
01:10:15.100 --> 01:10:16.540
There's some good bloopers from that, too.
那集还有一些很棒的NG镜头。

1732
01:10:17.000 --> 01:10:20.760
Listen, there was a deleted scene as Dwight is poaching everyone's clients.
听着，有个删减片段是关于德怀特挖走所有人客户的。

1733
01:10:21.060 --> 01:10:28.620
He really crosses the line with Ryan because Ryan's uncle chooses Dwight over the Michael
他真的惹恼了瑞安，因为瑞安的叔叔选择了德怀特，而不是迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司。

1734
01:10:28.620 --> 01:10:29.680
Scott Paper Company.
什么？

1735
01:10:29.880 --> 01:10:30.120
What?
什么？

1736
01:10:30.420 --> 01:10:30.580
Yeah.
没错。

1737
01:10:30.720 --> 01:10:32.280
And there's some really good Pam sass.
而且帕姆有一些非常犀利的吐槽。

1738
01:10:32.440 --> 01:10:33.140
We got to hear it.
我们得听听。

1739
01:10:34.080 --> 01:10:35.800
Dwight just got Howard family dry cleaners.
德怀特刚拿下了霍华德家族的干洗店。

1740
01:10:36.860 --> 01:10:37.580
Uncle Dave?
戴夫叔叔？

1741
01:10:37.720 --> 01:10:39.480
The jerk is undercutting us big time.
那个混蛋在大幅压价抢生意。

1742
01:10:39.720 --> 01:10:43.540
He is actually taking a loss and paying the difference out of pocket.
他实际上是在亏本经营，自掏腰包补差价。

1743
01:10:43.700 --> 01:10:44.420
That's my family.
那可是我的家人。

1744
01:10:45.440 --> 01:10:48.880
When you mess with my family, I can't be responsible for my actions.
当你招惹我的家人时，我可没法保证我会做出什么事来。

1745
01:10:49.560 --> 01:10:51.600
When are you ever responsible for your actions?
你什么时候对自己的行为负责过？

1746
01:10:51.740 --> 01:10:52.740
Get off my ass, you hag.
别烦我，你这老巫婆。

1747
01:10:52.900 --> 01:10:53.580
Hey, hey, hey.
嘿，嘿，嘿。

1748
01:10:53.740 --> 01:10:55.080
Something about that seems inappropriate.
这话听着有点不妥。

1749
01:10:56.680 --> 01:10:58.900
Something about that seems inappropriate.
这话听着有点不妥。

1750
01:10:59.020 --> 01:11:00.580
You can't put his finger on it.
你就是说不出哪里不对劲。

1751
01:11:00.840 --> 01:11:04.140
I love the Ryan-Pam rivalry.
我喜欢瑞安和帕姆之间的竞争。

1752
01:11:04.460 --> 01:11:06.020
I just live for it.
我简直太爱看了。

1753
01:11:06.560 --> 01:11:07.700
I love it, too.
我也很喜欢。

1754
01:11:08.100 --> 01:11:12.200
I mean, I just loved working with these guys for this period of time.
我是说，我真的很喜欢这段时间能和这些人一起工作。

1755
01:11:12.300 --> 01:11:13.540
I bet it was so much fun.
我敢说那一定很有趣。

1756
01:11:13.540 --> 01:11:21.000
Well, now we're going to get into a pretty fun bit where Michael is going to walk in to
好了，现在我们要进入一个非常有趣的桥段，迈克尔要走进

1757
01:11:21.000 --> 01:11:23.740
HarperCollins with Dwight on the phone.
哈珀柯林斯出版社，而德怀特还在电话那头。

1758
01:11:23.900 --> 01:11:27.020
He's like, I'm going to let you listen to me still, your biggest client.
他说，我要让你继续听着，我是你最大的客户。

1759
01:11:27.440 --> 01:11:30.420
And Dwight's like, no, and takes off.
德怀特说，不行，然后就挂了。

1760
01:11:30.700 --> 01:11:33.280
And he gets in the car all the while listening.
他一边开车一边还在听着。

1761
01:11:33.680 --> 01:11:35.320
That was so funny.
那段太搞笑了。

1762
01:11:35.460 --> 01:11:38.540
Rain in the car when he was like, paper is the manure.
雷恩在车里说“纸就是肥料”的时候。

1763
01:11:39.240 --> 01:11:43.750
And on time, I wrote down that quote, too.
当时我也记下了那句台词。

1764
01:11:43.750 --> 01:11:45.490
Do I need that on a mug?
我需要把它印在马克杯上吗？

1765
01:11:45.650 --> 01:11:47.010
We might need it on a mug.
我们或许真该把它印在杯子上。

1766
01:11:47.150 --> 01:11:48.350
Paper is the manure.
纸就是肥料。

1767
01:11:50.190 --> 01:11:52.470
We had a fan question from Sydney S.
我们收到一个来自悉尼·S的粉丝提问，

1768
01:11:52.610 --> 01:11:55.130
who said, how did you guys film that scene of Dwight
她问，你们是怎么拍摄德怀特

1769
01:11:55.130 --> 01:11:57.190
driving to Mr. Schofield's office?
开车去斯科菲尔德先生办公室那场戏的？

1770
01:11:57.450 --> 01:11:59.570
Was Steve really on the other end of the phone?
史蒂夫真的在电话那头吗？

1771
01:12:00.490 --> 01:12:02.970
No, Steve was not on the other end of the phone.
不，史蒂夫当时并不在电话那头。

1772
01:12:03.710 --> 01:12:05.850
And I talked with Randy about this.
我和兰迪聊过这件事。

1773
01:12:06.430 --> 01:12:07.750
Rain is really driving.
雷恩是真的在开车。

1774
01:12:08.010 --> 01:12:08.870
He's free driving.
他是自由驾驶。

1775
01:12:09.130 --> 01:12:10.770
He is not hooked up to anything.
他没有连接任何辅助设备。

1776
01:12:10.770 --> 01:12:13.750
It looked like it to me, just the way he pulled into the parking lot.
我看的时候觉得是，尤其是他开进停车场的那种方式。

1777
01:12:13.990 --> 01:12:15.330
Yeah, the whole time.
是的，全程都是。

1778
01:12:15.610 --> 01:12:18.670
So they had LAPD officers on motorcycles.
所以他们安排了洛杉矶警局的摩托车警官。

1779
01:12:19.130 --> 01:12:22.490
So no one would sort of interfere with the shot or rain driving.
这样就不会有人干扰拍摄或雷恩的驾驶。

1780
01:12:22.750 --> 01:12:23.490
Yes, correct.
没错，是这样。

1781
01:12:23.730 --> 01:12:26.810
And there's also a crew van following behind.
而且后面还有一辆剧组的面包车跟着。

1782
01:12:27.250 --> 01:12:29.010
But here's how they got that shot.
但他们是这样拍到那个镜头的。

1783
01:12:29.430 --> 01:12:31.990
Matt Soane, our camera operator, was in the front seat.
我们的摄影师马特·索恩坐在前排座位上。

1784
01:12:32.410 --> 01:12:32.890
Oh.
哦。

1785
01:12:33.070 --> 01:12:33.670
Filming rain.
拍摄雷恩。

1786
01:12:34.090 --> 01:12:37.510
Our sound engineer, Ben Patrick, was in the back seat recording sound.
我们的录音师本·帕特里克坐在后座录音。

1787
01:12:37.510 --> 01:12:40.630
And our director, Paul Feig, was also in the back seat.
我们的导演保罗·费格也坐在后座。

1788
01:12:40.990 --> 01:12:43.190
That was not a big back seat.
那后座可不宽敞。

1789
01:12:43.310 --> 01:12:44.610
I have been in that car.
我坐过那辆车。

1790
01:12:44.810 --> 01:12:45.970
That is tiny.
空间非常小。

1791
01:12:46.270 --> 01:12:46.830
I know.
我知道。

1792
01:12:47.250 --> 01:12:50.790
And Randy said, we did not have a two-way phone setup.
兰迪说，我们当时没有双向通话的设备。

1793
01:12:51.030 --> 01:12:52.590
It was just too unreliable.
那太不可靠了。

1794
01:12:52.950 --> 01:12:59.370
And so Randy's guess is that Paul Feig was reading Steve's dialogue so that Rain could react to it.
所以兰迪推测是保罗·费格在念史蒂夫的台词，好让雷恩做出反应。

1795
01:12:59.450 --> 01:12:59.630
Yeah.
没错。

1796
01:13:00.110 --> 01:13:00.550
Amazing.
太神奇了。

1797
01:13:01.030 --> 01:13:03.050
I wish we had a picture of those four guys in the car.
真希望我们有那四个人挤在车里的照片。

1798
01:13:03.050 --> 01:13:07.130
Can we talk about what happens when Dwight arrives at Mr. Schofield's office?
我们可以聊聊德怀特到达斯科菲尔德先生办公室后发生了什么吗？

1799
01:13:07.370 --> 01:13:07.810
Finally.
终于到了。

1800
01:13:08.110 --> 01:13:09.230
I lived for this.
我太期待这一段了。

1801
01:13:09.450 --> 01:13:12.850
I had to know if this was scripted or improvised.
我必须得知道这是写好的剧本还是即兴发挥的。

1802
01:13:13.010 --> 01:13:15.050
So Dwight is going to run in.
所以德怀特要跑进来了。

1803
01:13:15.170 --> 01:13:17.370
First of all, he's changing into his mustard shirt.
首先，他换上了那件芥末黄衬衫。

1804
01:13:17.470 --> 01:13:18.330
I loved that detail.
我特别喜欢这个细节。

1805
01:13:18.530 --> 01:13:19.210
I loved that detail.
我特别喜欢这个细节。

1806
01:13:19.430 --> 01:13:23.430
And then when he gets to the receptionist, he does this crazy spin move.
然后当他走到前台时，他做了一个疯狂的旋转动作。

1807
01:13:23.650 --> 01:13:26.110
And then Dwight says, spin move.
接着德怀特说了句“旋转动作”。

1808
01:13:26.530 --> 01:13:28.590
And I was like, did Rain improvise that?
当时我就在想，这是雷恩即兴发挥的吗？

1809
01:13:28.750 --> 01:13:29.330
I've got to know.
我一定要搞清楚。

1810
01:13:29.670 --> 01:13:31.250
Jenna, it was 100% in the script.
珍娜，这百分之百是剧本里写好的。

1811
01:13:31.250 --> 01:13:34.470
Everything, even the spin move, all of it.
所有的一切，包括那个旋转动作，全都是。

1812
01:13:34.670 --> 01:13:40.630
I found an old interview with Rain where he said that one time he did a somersault.
我翻到了一篇雷恩的旧采访，他说有一次他做了一个空翻。

1813
01:13:41.590 --> 01:13:44.950
And he said he thought that it would look extra stealthy.
他说他当时觉得那样看起来会格外隐蔽。

1814
01:13:45.150 --> 01:13:50.470
When they watched it back, it looked, quote, like a manatee doing ballet at SeaWorld.
但当他们回看录像时，引用他的话，看起来就像“一只在海洋世界跳芭蕾的海牛”。

1815
01:13:51.890 --> 01:13:54.430
He also said they did about five takes.
他还说他们大概拍了五条才过。

1816
01:13:54.690 --> 01:13:59.330
I also have a little guest star breakdown for Mr. Schofield's receptioniSt.
我还整理了一份关于斯科菲尔德先生前台的小客串演员资料。

1817
01:13:59.330 --> 01:14:07.230
She was played by Angela Campola Sanders, who was our casting associate on The Office since season four.
她由安吉拉·坎波拉·桑德斯饰演，她是《办公室》第四季以来的选角助理。

1818
01:14:07.470 --> 01:14:09.090
This is her only acting credit.
这是她唯一的演艺作品。

1819
01:14:09.290 --> 01:14:09.610
That's awesome.
那太棒了。

1820
01:14:09.610 --> 01:14:12.630
But she played Mr. Schofield's receptioniSt.
但她确实演了斯科菲尔德先生的前台。

1821
01:14:12.870 --> 01:14:16.810
Pretty much everyone in our casting office made it into the episode at some point.
我们选角办公室的几乎每个人都在这一集中露过脸。

1822
01:14:16.910 --> 01:14:17.490
I love that.
我喜欢这样。

1823
01:14:17.650 --> 01:14:18.110
I do too.
我也是。

1824
01:14:18.790 --> 01:14:26.010
Dwight is about to dig himself into a big old hole because he doesn't understand Michael's Rolodex or Michael's color coding info.
德怀特快要给自己挖个大坑了，因为他根本不懂迈克尔的通讯录或颜色编码信息。

1825
01:14:26.470 --> 01:14:29.770
Michael has a talking head where he says, I color code all my info.
迈克尔有个单人访谈，他说：“我把所有信息都做了颜色编码。”

1826
01:14:29.950 --> 01:14:31.170
I wrote gay son in green.
“我用绿色写了‘同性恋儿子’。”

1827
01:14:31.370 --> 01:14:32.110
Green means go.
“绿色代表通行。”

1828
01:14:32.310 --> 01:14:34.350
So I know to go ahead and shut up about it.
“所以我知道该继续说下去，还是闭嘴不谈。”

1829
01:14:34.850 --> 01:14:35.130
Yes.
没错。

1830
01:14:35.210 --> 01:14:36.270
And orange means orange.
“而橙色就代表橙色。”

1831
01:14:36.390 --> 01:14:37.510
You glad you didn't bring it up.
“代表你庆幸自己没提这茬。”

1832
01:14:37.770 --> 01:14:39.390
Most colors mean don't say it.
“大多数颜色都意味着别说出来。”

1833
01:14:39.830 --> 01:14:40.070
Yeah.
是啊。

1834
01:14:40.430 --> 01:14:41.570
But Dwight doesn't know that.
但德怀特不知道这一点。

1835
01:14:42.290 --> 01:14:42.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1836
01:14:42.690 --> 01:14:47.410
So Dwight is basically saying all the things that are color coded to not be said.
所以德怀特基本上把所有颜色编码里不该说的话全说了出来。

1837
01:14:47.610 --> 01:14:47.810
Right.
没错。

1838
01:14:47.810 --> 01:14:57.570
Well, before we wrap up this heavy competition between Mike, wait, this episode, that's the champagne.
好吧，在我们结束这场迈克之间的激烈竞争之前，等等，这一集，那是香槟。

1839
01:14:57.750 --> 01:14:58.070
I know.
我知道。

1840
01:14:58.170 --> 01:15:01.290
And the champagne, you have a nickname for everyone in your champagne brain.
还有香槟，你在“香槟大脑”里给每个人都起了绰号。

1841
01:15:01.390 --> 01:15:01.850
Mike.
迈克。

1842
01:15:02.030 --> 01:15:02.410
Mike.
迈克。

1843
01:15:02.790 --> 01:15:03.170
Dwighty.
德怀特。

1844
01:15:05.590 --> 01:15:06.270
Okay.
好吧。

1845
01:15:07.410 --> 01:15:13.170
I think we should go back and wrap up this Andy Jim storyline.
我觉得我们应该回去把安迪和吉姆的故事线收个尾。

1846
01:15:13.590 --> 01:15:13.810
Okay.
好的。

1847
01:15:14.010 --> 01:15:16.330
We both had to stop drinking champagne, by the way.
顺便说一下，我们俩都得停止喝香槟了。

1848
01:15:16.850 --> 01:15:17.650
We did.
确实。

1849
01:15:18.030 --> 01:15:20.350
It just, it's so interesting.
这真的，太有意思了。

1850
01:15:20.530 --> 01:15:22.490
Scotch and Splenda was like, woo-boo, woo-boo.
苏格兰威士忌加代糖简直是，呜呼，呜呼。

1851
01:15:22.650 --> 01:15:25.050
But champagne were like, I can't talk right now.
但香槟就像是说，我现在没法说话。

1852
01:15:25.290 --> 01:15:25.690
Yeah.
是啊。

1853
01:15:25.810 --> 01:15:28.250
I still really do love the Scotch and Splenda.
我依然真的很喜欢苏格兰威士忌加代糖。

1854
01:15:28.470 --> 01:15:28.890
Me too.
我也是。

1855
01:15:28.890 --> 01:15:29.930
I have to say.
我得说。

1856
01:15:29.930 --> 01:15:31.110
It's a really good drink.
这确实是一款好喝的饮品。

1857
01:15:31.110 --> 01:15:36.530
And we got some letters from people who said it's basically an old fashioned if we'd added a few orange bitters.
我们收到了一些观众来信，说如果我们加点橙味苦精，它基本上就是一杯古典鸡尾酒了。

1858
01:15:36.670 --> 01:15:38.150
And that's what it tasted like to me.
我喝起来也是这种感觉。

1859
01:15:38.250 --> 01:15:38.510
That's right.
没错。

1860
01:15:38.810 --> 01:15:40.770
Because I guess you would add like a sugar.
因为我想你得加点糖之类的东西。

1861
01:15:41.050 --> 01:15:41.410
Yeah.
是啊。

1862
01:15:41.770 --> 01:15:45.350
A muddled kind of sugary syrup to the Scotch.
往苏格兰威士忌里加点捣碎的糖浆之类的。

1863
01:15:45.350 --> 01:15:45.530
Right.
对。

1864
01:15:45.530 --> 01:15:47.550
And so that's what the Splenda is doing.
所以代糖起的就是这个作用。

1865
01:15:48.030 --> 01:15:48.190
Yeah.
是啊。

1866
01:15:48.610 --> 01:15:50.650
But champagne just makes us go, what?
但香槟只会让我们觉得，什么？

1867
01:15:50.750 --> 01:15:51.550
What are we talking about?
我们在说什么？

1868
01:15:51.690 --> 01:15:52.030
What's happening?
发生了什么？

1869
01:15:52.030 --> 01:15:52.410
I know.
我知道。

1870
01:15:52.670 --> 01:15:52.850
Okay.
好吧。

1871
01:15:53.330 --> 01:15:53.930
All right.
行吧。

1872
01:15:54.970 --> 01:15:55.390
See?
你看？

1873
01:15:55.650 --> 01:15:56.170
I know.
我知道。

1874
01:15:56.290 --> 01:15:57.430
I'm like, what am I talking about?
我都在想，我到底在说什么？

1875
01:15:57.610 --> 01:15:57.790
Okay.
好吧。

1876
01:15:57.990 --> 01:15:59.130
So Andy and Jim.
所以安迪和吉姆。

1877
01:16:00.290 --> 01:16:03.550
Andy is going to tell the whole bullpen that Jim is upset.
安迪要告诉整个办公区的人说吉姆很心烦。

1878
01:16:04.830 --> 01:16:09.810
And Phyllis is going to be like, Andy, I think Jim is just messing with you.
然后菲利斯会说，安迪，我觉得吉姆只是在逗你玩。

1879
01:16:10.050 --> 01:16:16.090
And then there's that smug shot of Jim in the kitchen looking out through the blinds with that grin on his face.
然后就是吉姆在厨房里透过百叶窗往外看，脸上带着那种自鸣得意的笑容的镜头。

1880
01:16:16.090 --> 01:16:21.250
We had a fan question from Raya H and Poonet B.
我们收到了来自Raya H和Poonet B的粉丝提问。

1881
01:16:21.730 --> 01:16:25.170
Can we talk about how douchey Jim is being in this episode?
我们能聊聊吉姆在这一集里有多混蛋吗？

1882
01:16:25.710 --> 01:16:28.790
Andy was being really supportive and genuinely cared for Jim.
安迪当时真的很支持吉姆，而且是真心关心他。

1883
01:16:28.950 --> 01:16:35.150
And while Andy's concern might have been misguided or nosy, I think it came from a good place.
虽然安迪的关心可能有点找错方向或者多管闲事，但我认为他的出发点是好的。

1884
01:16:35.430 --> 01:16:43.890
We'd really like to get your take on this prank that Jim pulls on Andy because we think the prank might have been a little mean-spirited.
我们真的很想听听你们对吉姆捉弄安迪这件事的看法，因为我们觉得这个恶作剧可能有点恶意。

1885
01:16:44.550 --> 01:16:45.830
I didn't care for it.
我不喜欢这个恶作剧。

1886
01:16:46.090 --> 01:16:46.810
I didn't either.
我也不喜欢。

1887
01:16:46.930 --> 01:16:48.930
I do think this is a mean-spirited joke.
我觉得这确实是一个恶意的玩笑。

1888
01:16:49.110 --> 01:16:50.930
I mean, we already know I don't like pranks.
我是说，大家都知道我不喜欢恶作剧。

1889
01:16:51.130 --> 01:16:54.370
And I don't love especially pranks that-
而且我特别不喜欢那种……

1890
01:16:54.370 --> 01:16:55.310
At someone's expense.
以牺牲他人为代价的。

1891
01:16:55.390 --> 01:16:56.750
That play with their emotions.
那种玩弄别人感情的。

1892
01:16:56.990 --> 01:16:57.130
Right.
没错。

1893
01:16:57.330 --> 01:17:04.030
I think it was too big of a reaction to Andy's kind of nosy meddling.
我觉得对于安迪那种爱管闲事的干预，吉姆的反应太过火了。

1894
01:17:04.290 --> 01:17:07.490
And he does have this nice speech, Jim, at the end to Andy.
而且吉姆在最后确实对安迪发表了一番不错的演讲。

1895
01:17:07.530 --> 01:17:11.950
He's like, listen, I know Angela broke your heart, but you're going to find someone else.
他说，听着，我知道安吉拉伤了你的心，但你会找到别人的。

1896
01:17:12.050 --> 01:17:12.850
You really will.
你真的会找到的。

1897
01:17:13.310 --> 01:17:17.270
So I feel like that was the moment where the writers were like, you know, Jim's not a bad guy.
所以我感觉那是编剧们想表达，你知道的，吉姆并不是个坏人。

1898
01:17:17.490 --> 01:17:21.350
Maybe he was trying to show Andy something, but I just didn't like the prank.
也许他当时是想教安迪点什么，但我就是不喜欢这个恶作剧。

1899
01:17:21.710 --> 01:17:22.390
Me either.
我也不喜欢。

1900
01:17:22.670 --> 01:17:22.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1901
01:17:23.210 --> 01:17:24.850
Well, I'm glad we discussed that.
好吧，很高兴我们讨论了这件事。

1902
01:17:24.990 --> 01:17:25.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1903
01:17:25.110 --> 01:17:25.750
We're with you.
我们支持你。

1904
01:17:25.750 --> 01:17:29.310
So this episode ends with more cheeseball fun.
所以这一集在更多奶酪球的乐趣中结束。

1905
01:17:29.810 --> 01:17:34.270
Michael, Ryan, and Pam, they're trying to see how many cheese puffs can they fit in their mouth.
迈克尔、瑞安和帕姆，他们想看看嘴里能塞进多少个奶酪球。

1906
01:17:34.530 --> 01:17:34.910
32.
32个。

1907
01:17:35.290 --> 01:17:36.190
That's the record.
那是纪录。

1908
01:17:36.350 --> 01:17:36.510
Yeah.
没错。

1909
01:17:36.510 --> 01:17:42.070
And then the phone rings and Michael answers it and he's got a mouthful of cheese puffs and we're all laughing.
然后电话响了，迈克尔接起电话，嘴里塞满了奶酪球，我们都笑个不停。

1910
01:17:42.390 --> 01:17:48.630
And while this is happening, you can hear a Michael talking head where he's saying he wanted to start a company and not a war.
就在这时，你可以听到迈克尔的采访片段，他说他想创办一家公司，而不是发动一场战争。

1911
01:17:49.290 --> 01:17:52.330
Well, this talking head was added later.
嗯，这个采访片段是后来加进去的。

1912
01:17:52.610 --> 01:17:54.230
This was not in the original script.
这不在最初的剧本里。

1913
01:17:54.910 --> 01:17:58.650
Steve shot this a couple weeks after we shot the original episode.
史蒂夫是在我们拍摄完原剧集几周后补拍的。

1914
01:17:58.650 --> 01:18:02.970
And all of this footage of us doing this cheese puffs bit.
还有所有我们玩奶酪球的镜头。

1915
01:18:03.110 --> 01:18:03.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1916
01:18:03.510 --> 01:18:06.950
This was originally going to be at the end of the cold open.
这原本打算放在冷开场结束时。

1917
01:18:07.170 --> 01:18:09.810
So it was all of that was going to live at the top of the episode.
所以这一切原本打算放在剧集开头。

1918
01:18:10.030 --> 01:18:10.470
Yes.
是的。

1919
01:18:10.470 --> 01:18:16.510
But they thought it would be funnier to end the cold open on Pam getting the cheese puffs while she's yawning.
但他们觉得以帕姆打着哈欠吃奶酪球来结束冷开场会更有趣。

1920
01:18:17.110 --> 01:18:22.450
And then they gave this episode this new tag with the cheese ball bit.
然后他们给这一集加了这个新的结尾片段。

1921
01:18:22.730 --> 01:18:25.090
This was not the original tag for the episode.
这并不是这一集最初的结尾片段。

1922
01:18:25.090 --> 01:18:29.990
So instead of this bookend of cheese puffs at the beginning and end, there was a tag.
所以，原本开头和结尾都有奶酪球的呼应，后来变成了一个结尾片段。

1923
01:18:30.530 --> 01:18:31.910
And we did film it.
而且我们确实拍了。

1924
01:18:32.030 --> 01:18:33.430
And I want to share it with you guys.
我想和你们分享一下。

1925
01:18:34.050 --> 01:18:38.110
So Andy is in the conference room and he is selling off his wedding stuff.
安迪在会议室里，他正在变卖他的婚礼用品。

1926
01:18:38.270 --> 01:18:38.990
He's determined.
他很坚定。

1927
01:18:39.790 --> 01:18:42.410
Well, you know, he didn't get buyers from Jim and Pam.
嗯，你知道，吉姆和帕姆没买他的东西。

1928
01:18:42.630 --> 01:18:45.470
So in the tag, he's selling it to the rest of the gang.
所以在结尾片段里，他在向其他人兜售。

1929
01:18:45.650 --> 01:18:47.390
And they're all bidding on things.
他们都在竞价购买。

1930
01:18:47.810 --> 01:18:49.450
Stanley buys the rice bags.
斯坦利买了那些米袋。

1931
01:18:49.630 --> 01:18:52.030
And Creed decides to get in on the action, too.
克里德也决定参与进来。

1932
01:18:52.250 --> 01:18:53.930
I thought we had to hear a little bit of it.
我想我们得听听那段内容。

1933
01:18:55.090 --> 01:18:56.270
Why are you here, Stanley?
你来这儿干什么，斯坦利？

1934
01:18:56.710 --> 01:18:57.970
I'm here for the rice.
我是来买米的。

1935
01:18:58.230 --> 01:18:58.530
Boom.
砰。

1936
01:18:58.750 --> 01:18:59.090
Sold.
成交。

1937
01:18:59.310 --> 01:19:00.090
100 bags of rice.
100袋米。

1938
01:19:00.190 --> 01:19:00.630
Stanley Hudson.
斯坦利·哈德森。

1939
01:19:00.930 --> 01:19:04.210
Creed, how would you like a crispy new tuxedo for your funeral?
克里德，你想要一套崭新的燕尾服作为你的葬礼服吗？

1940
01:19:04.430 --> 01:19:05.670
I'll take the bottom half.
我要下半身就行。

1941
01:19:07.030 --> 01:19:08.930
I want to go out the same way I came in.
我想以我出生时的方式离开。

1942
01:19:09.110 --> 01:19:09.550
Shirtless.
光着上身。

1943
01:19:10.930 --> 01:19:15.290
And everyone else starts making bids, too, asking questions on things.
其他人也开始竞价，并询问关于物品的问题。

1944
01:19:16.170 --> 01:19:20.690
Angela is not in the scene, but she walks by and had this talking head.
安吉拉不在现场，但她走过时有这样一个采访片段。

1945
01:19:20.690 --> 01:19:21.970
It was in the shooting draft.
这在拍摄初稿里。

1946
01:19:22.370 --> 01:19:24.090
